# Push and CI/CD are operator-owned

The human operator (not the coding agent) runs git push and CI/CD.

The agent must **not**:

- `git push` (any remote, any branch)
- run `scripts/git-autocommit.ps1` (it commits **and** pushes)
- trigger GitHub Actions (`workflow_dispatch`, `gh workflow run`, reruns)
- log into Yandex Container Registry, build/push images, or run `scripts/deploy_containers.sh`

The agent **may** edit files and run local checks (`npm run typecheck`, tests). Commit only when the operator explicitly asks, and even then stop before push.

When a change needs to land on `main` or go through CI, say so and leave staging/commit/push to the operator (VS Code task **Git: auto add+commit+push**, or their own git).
